own tasty granola bars right at home.\n\nThis recipe is for chewy granola bars.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (120 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) soft [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* ¾ cup (180 g) brown [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ⅓ cup (80 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Corn Syrup|corn syrup]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n* 3 ½ cups (900 g) uncooked [[Cookbook:Oats|oats]]\n* 1 cup (240 g) [[Cookbook:Chocolate Chips|chocolate chips]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 350°F (180°C).\n# Grease 13 x 9-inch (30 x 23 cm) [[Cookbook:Baking Pan|baking pan]].\n# Combine butter, sugar, and corn syrup.\n# Mix in egg and vanilla.\n# Stir in oats and chocolate chips.\n# Spread mixture in prepared pan.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] 20–22 minutes.\n# Let cool. Cut into bars, and enjoy.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* For extra flavor, add a desired amount of nuts and raisin.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using oat]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chocolate]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Snacks recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Confectionery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn syrup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Granola Bars","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup (120 g) soft butter or margarine","sourceText":"½ cup (120 g) soft butter or margarine","amountText":"½ cup (120 g) soft butter or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup (180 g) brown sugar","sourceText":"¾ cup (180 g) brown sugar","amountText":"¾ cup (180 g) brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"⅓ cup (80 ml) corn syrup","sourceText":"⅓ c